      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Key Management Options**\n\nI'm evaluating key management service providers. Currently, Google Cloud KMS looks promising for decrypting ciphertext with a managed key. I plan to create a Python script, `decrypt_payload.py`, to handle the decryption.\n\n\n**Developing Decryption Script**\n\nI'm now focused on the practical implementation. I'm building `decrypt_payload.py` with Google Cloud KMS. The core logic will use `google.cloud.kms_v1` for the KMS client. I'll include placeholders for key details like the resource name, which should ideally be configurable via environment variables, to keep things simple for this initial version.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865543249,
          "start": 1789865540614
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc4cbc06001xkTl3B6gig2p5q",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc4cb839001YplONuhtYmPrTr",
      "session_id": "ses_f43b347d6ffeBLrOW6jKweBGnS",
